<title>BELGIUM: EU clears Siemens stake in car lock firm.</title>
<headline>EU clears Siemens stake in car lock firm.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had cleared plans by German industrial giant Siemens AG to take a stake in German company Huelsbeck &amp; Fuerst GmbH.</p>
<p>Siemens said in January it would acquire 25 percent of Huelsbeck &amp; Fuerst GmbH and the same stake in Huelsbeck &amp; Fuerst partner Huf Industrieverwaltung GmbH as part of a plan to boost its position in the market for keyless automobile locks.</p>
<p>The two companies manufacture car door handles, steering wheel locks and other mechanical components for car entry systems.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
